What is an Exception?
An exception is an unexpected event that disrupts the normal flow of a program.

Error = System-level issue (JVM crash, OutOfMemory)
Exception = Something you can handle in code

Hierarchy:
Throwable
   ├── Error (JVM-level, not recoverable)
   └── Exception
         ├── Checked Exception
         └── Unchecked Exception (Runtime)


Checked vs Unchecked:
| Type          | Examples                                                         | When Checked | Needs `try/catch` or `throws`? |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------ |
| **Checked**   | IOException, SQLException                                        | Compile-time | ✅ Yes                          |
| **Unchecked** | NullPointerException, ArithmeticException, ArrayIndexOutOfBounds | Runtime      | ❌ No (optional)                |


// Checked Exception
FileReader f = new FileReader("abc.txt");  // must handle using try/catch

// Unchecked Exception
int x = 10 / 0;  // ArithmeticException

finally is always executed — even if there’s an exception or return statement (except when JVM exits).

throw and throws:
| Keyword  | Purpose                                                                      | Example                                          |
| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `throw`  | Used to **manually throw** an exception                                      | `throw new ArithmeticException("Invalid calc");` |
| `throws` | Used in method signature to **declare** that a method may throw an exception | `void readFile() throws IOException`             |


| Keyword   | Meaning                         |
| --------- | ------------------------------- |
| try       | Code that might throw exception |
| catch     | Handles the exception           |
| finally   | Always executes (cleanup code)  |
| throw     | Manually throw an exception     |
| throws    | Declares exception in method    |
| Exception | Recoverable issue               |
| Error     | Serious system-level failure    |
